   "text": {
    "L1": "Gilli danda is a traditional game played with two sticks: a gilli and a danda.",
    "L2": "The poem says you do not need costly toys to have fun; two old sticks can bring lots of joy.",
    "L3": "First, place the gilli on the ground. Then tap one end so it springs up.",
    "L4": "Whack! Hit the gilli hard with the danda, and watch it fly high and fast.",
    "L5": "The gilli flies as if on wings, but this is a comparison, not a fact about real wings.",
    "L6": "After it lands, players count or measure how far it went to see who is winning.",
    "L7": "The exclamation mark makes Whack sound sudden and loud, so stress that word when you recite.",
    "L8": "Remember the order: place, tap, hit, then measure. Simple play can give great joy."
   },
